📊 What is Data? | Understanding the Data Hierarchy

Data is the foundation of modern decision-making. From customer information and sales records to website activity and business performance, data helps organizations understand what is happening, why it is happening, and what they should do next.

🔹 Data Hierarchy / Career Path

Data Analyst → Data Engineer → Data Scientist → AI/ML Engineer

Each role works with data at a different level:

📌 Data Analyst — Analyzes data, creates reports and dashboards, identifies trends, and helps businesses make better decisions.

📌 Data Engineer — Builds and maintains the systems, pipelines, and infrastructure required to collect, transform, store, and deliver data.

📌 Data Scientist — Uses statistics, programming, and advanced analytics to discover patterns, make predictions, and solve complex business problems.

📌 AI/ML Engineer — Develops, deploys, and maintains machine learning and AI systems that learn from data and enable intelligent automation.

🚀 Understanding this hierarchy helps you see how raw data moves from collection → processing → analysis → prediction → intelligent automation.
